From 54104dfda6dce930a574d4550fa4216e6d6d5c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:42:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 217/237] ASoC: mediatek: Add the MT6858 AFE platform driver

The MT6858 AFE shares the MT8189's memif, IRQ, ADDA and eTDM register
layout: of the 812 register fields the MT8189 driver uses, all that
exist on the MT6858 have the same values in MediaTek's MT6858 register
map. Derive the driver from mt8189, without the blocks the MT6858 lacks
(I2S0, TDM, HDMI, AP DMIC, MTKAIFv4/ADDA6 and the custom TDM IRQ), and
with what the MT6858 does differently, from MediaTek's GPLv2 driver:

- the 26 MHz request is bit 2 of AFE_SPM_CONTROL_REQ, not bit 0;
- the eTDM slave-select values follow the MT6858's IN1/2/4, OUT1/2/4;
- I2SOUT1 has no clock pads and runs on I2SIN1's BCK and LRCK, so
  I2SOUT1 shares I2SIN1 by default;
- the eTDM in2latch and out2latch timings.

The MT8189's MT6363 VS1 voter was never wired up (no PMIC regmap is
ever set), so it is not carried over.

Tested on the Jolla Phone (2026): the AFE probes behind the AUDIO power
domain, and 4 s of DL0 into I2SOUT1 take 4.1 s with 33 period IRQs.
Capture through the ADDA has no data yet (see the MT6369 codec).
